From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaq Question <zaquestion@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mark a floating focused client in the layout symbol

dwl already publishes the focused client's floating state over ipc
(zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_floating, added by 0001), but waybar 0.12's
dwl/window module ignores that event -- its only format replacements are
{title}, {app_id} and {layout}, and {layout} comes from the layout_symbol
event. So there is no way to tell from the bar whether the focused window
was floated with Mod+Shift+Space.

Suffix the symbol sent over ipc with "~" when the focused client is
floating: "[]=" tiled, "[]=~" with a floating window focused. The monitor's
own ltsymbol is left untouched, so nothing else (dwl's internal state, the
floating event itself) changes.
---
 dwl.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dwl.c b/dwl.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/dwl.c
+++ b/dwl.c
@@ -1458,6 +1458,7 @@
 	Client *c, *focused;
 	int tagmask, state, numclients, focused_client, tag;
 	const char *title, *appid;
+	char ltsymbol[LENGTH(monitor->ltsymbol) + 2];
 	focused = focustop(monitor);
 	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_active(ipc_output->resource, monitor == selmon);

@@ -1484,10 +1485,16 @@
 	title = focused ? client_get_title(focused) : "";
 	appid = focused ? client_get_appid(focused) : "";

+	/* Bars get the floating state below, but waybar 0.12's dwl/window module
+	 * ignores that event -- it only renders the layout symbol. Fold the two
+	 * together so a floated client is visible: "[]=" tiled, "[]=~" floating. */
+	snprintf(ltsymbol, sizeof ltsymbol, "%s%s", monitor->ltsymbol,
+			focused && focused->isfloating ? "~" : "");
+
 	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_layout(ipc_output->resource, monitor->lt[monitor->sellt] - layouts);
 	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_title(ipc_output->resource, title);
 	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_appid(ipc_output->resource, appid);
-	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_layout_symbol(ipc_output->resource, monitor->ltsymbol);
+	zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_layout_symbol(ipc_output->resource, ltsymbol);
 	if (wl_resource_get_version(ipc_output->resource) >= ZDWL_IPC_OUTPUT_V2_FULLSCREEN_SINCE_VERSION) {
 		zdwl_ipc_output_v2_send_fullscreen(ipc_output->resource, focused ? focused->isfullscreen : 0);
 	}
